{
  "info": {
    "name": "SOTWISE — GSS Checklist da Order (etapas order / pi / po)",
    "description": "Testa o endpoint que o GSS usa para atualizar as etapas do checklist da Order no SOTWISE:\n\n- `GET /api/orders/{id}/steps/{step}` — estado da etapa + revisões\n- `PATCH /api/orders/{id}/steps/{step}` — o dado que conclui a etapa\n\n`{id}` = UUID ou `po_number`. `{step}` = `order` (order_received_date) | `pi` (pi_status boolean: true = PI emitida, conclui; false = só grava + pi_status_date) | `po` (items[] de Factory × Category). `reason` opcional (motivo da revisão; sem ele grava \"Updated by GSS\"). Datas em Unix (segundos) — ou, legado, `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\nRegras (as mesmas da tela): o 1º dado conclui a etapa, os seguintes viram revisão (o original nunca se perde); o `completed_on` é sempre o dia da ÚLTIMA atualização (na PI, a data do status) e não se grava direto; valor idêntico não grava nada; campo de outra etapa → 400.\n\n**Como rodar:** environment **\"SOTWISE — GSS (prod)\"** (`base_url` + `api_token`). Rode a collection inteira no Runner, NA ORDEM: o passo 0 cria uma order de teste (`GSS-TEST-…`) e o último a apaga — nenhuma order real é tocada. O passo do PO usa `supplier_category_gss_id_1` do environment (se vazio, usa o default da collection).\n\nSwagger: `{{base_url}}/api/docs` → Orders → getOrderStep / patchOrderStep.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{api_token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "https://sot.gssdatahub.com",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "default_supplier_category_gss_id",
      "value": "11",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "test_po_number",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "test_order_id",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Setup — cria a order de teste (POST /api/orders) — 201",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/orders",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "orders"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Cria uma order descartável (gss_id/po_number com prefixo GSS-TEST-) para os testes não mexerem em nada real. É apagada no último passo.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"gss_id\": \"{{test_gss_id}}\",\n  \"po_number\": \"{{test_po_number}}\",\n  \"client_reference\": \"Postman — teste das etapas (descartável)\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const n = 'GSS-TEST-STEPS-' + Date.now();",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('test_gss_id', n);",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('test_po_number', n);"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('201 — order criada', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('test_order_id', b.data.id);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. GET order — etapa aberta — 200",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/orders/{{test_po_number}}/steps/order",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "orders",
            "{{test_po_number}}",
            "steps",
            "order"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
              "pm.test('aberta: completed_on null', () => pm.expect(d.completed_on).to.eql(null));",
              "pm.test('sem revisões', () => pm.expect(d.revisions).to.have.length(0));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. PATCH order — 1º Order received date conclui a etapa — 200",
      "request": {
        "method": "PATCH",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/orders/{{test_po_number}}/steps/order",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "orders",
            "{{test_po_number}}",
            "steps",
            "order"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"order_received_date\": {{d_received_1}}\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('d_received_1', Math.floor(new Date('2026-10-20T12:00:00Z').getTime() / 1000));"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
              "pm.test('concluída (completed_on preenchido)', () => pm.expect(d.completed_on).to.be.a('number'));",
              "pm.test('order_received_date gravado', () => pm.expect(d.order_received_date).to.eql(Number(pm.collectionVariables.get('d_received_1'))));",
              "pm.test('1 registro (o original)', () => pm.expect(d.revisions).to.have.length(1));",
              "pm.test('fonte = gss', () => pm.expect(d.revisions[0].source).to.eql('gss'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. PATCH order — revisão com motivo — 200",
      "request": {
        "method": "PATCH",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/orders/{{test_po_number}}/steps/order",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "orders",
            "{{test_po_number}}",
            "steps",
            "order"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"order_received_date\": {{d_received_2}},\n  \"reason\": \"Final PO re-sent by the client\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('d_received_2', Math.floor(new Date('2026-10-21T12:00:00Z').getTime() / 1000));"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
              "pm.test('2 registros: original + revisão', () => pm.expect(d.revisions).to.have.length(2));",
              "pm.test('motivo gravado', () => pm.expect(d.revisions[1].reason).to.eql('Final PO re-sent by the client'));",
              "pm.test('original preservado', () => pm.expect(d.revisions[0].new_date).to.eql(Number(pm.collectionVariables.get('d_received_1'))));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. PATCH order — mesmo valor não grava nada — 200",
      "request": {
        "method": "PATCH",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/orders/{{test_po_number}}/steps/order",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
